# AWPTCM-T44279 (218) Authentication&Security_... - Tri-Authentication
# Working log, run 1 -- tb277 / swi_d (AT-x960-56YSQ) -- group B, authmodes-2026-10-23T1304
# Tester: bench-runner subagent, 2026-10-23 16:29-16:38 NZDT (03:29-03:38 UTC)

## What the case asks

This case **does** have authored text in `ck.db` -- an objective, no steps:

> *"Confirm that dot1,MAC authentications is possible."*

TPS row **216 "Tri-Authentication" reads `Yes`**. The dispatch noted the discrepancy: the title
says *Tri*-Authentication, i.e. **three** methods (802.1X, MAC and **web**), while the authored
objective names only two -- and warned that the web limb goes beyond the objective, that
`httpq.py` does Basic auth only with no cookies or form handling, and that **the window was not
to be spent building an HTTP client**.

**No HTTP client was needed.** The AW+ web-authentication login page is a plain `POST` with two
fields and no cookie, no session token and no CSRF token, so `httpq.py --method POST --data`
drove it unchanged. **All three methods were therefore measured**, and all three authenticated
simultaneously on one port. The authored two-method objective is met with room to spare, and the
third limb is a measurement rather than a caveat.

Graded on the wire and on the DUT's own per-supplicant table; the key artefact is a single
`show auth supplicant brief` showing three supplicants Authenticated by **three different
methods at the same instant**, each one backed by a dataplane count.

