### Two rig facts worth recording

**1. `auth-web enable` AUTO-ADDS `auth forward arp`, `auth forward dhcp` and `auth forward
dns`, visibly, in the running-config.** Web authentication cannot work without them -- an
unauthenticated client must be able to ARP for the gateway, get an address and resolve a name
before it can reach a login page. This is the **opposite** of the silent-discard behaviour found
three times elsewhere in this group (T44277, T33369, T33362): here the DUT adds what the feature
needs and shows it. Recorded as the contrast case.

🔴 **It also forced a change of instrument mid-case.** The other four cases in this group used an
**ARP** request for the DUT's own address as the dataplane probe. With `auth forward arp` in
force, ARP is forwarded for **unauthenticated** supplicants too, so that probe can no longer
discriminate. **Every dataplane measurement in this case therefore uses ICMP echo** to
10.38.22.66 (`arpleg.py --icmp ... --gw-mac e0:1a:ea:d4:70:43`, with `--answer` so the DUT can
resolve the sender). ICMP is not in the forward list and is blocked until authorisation. The
instrument change is called out so the numbers in this log are not compared with the other four
cases' numbers as though they came from the same probe.

**2. The DUT attempts MAC authentication for EVERY new MAC before 802.1X.** Visible in the log
and it explains a timing difference measured below.

### The four MACs

| name | MAC | expected path |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **MAC X** | `02:0d:b9:00:42:79` | **MAC authentication** -- user `02-0d-b9-00-42-79` exists |
| **MAC Y** | `02:0d:b9:00:42:7a` | **802.1X** as `ckmulti1` -- no MAC user, so MAC auth must fail first |
| **MAC Z** | `02:0d:b9:00:42:7b` | **the CONTROL** -- no MAC user, and a wrong 802.1X password |
| **host eth4** | `00:0d:b9:55:77:0f` | **web authentication** as `ckweb` -- the box's own NIC |

